module gunbc.machine_intake.prior_life_capture_live

// THE LIVE PRIOR-LIFE ARCHIVE (PXE 1d-c). Where gunbc.machine_intake.prior_life_boundary classifies a
// supplied DRY world, this module READINGLY assembles the same CarrierCaptures from srv15's (ALTRAD8UD,
// OpenBMC 3.22.00) controller over the declared read-only ops, so a live arrival fold carries real prior
// life into PriorLifeBoundary instead of stopping there. Provenance: the design note approved by
// smart-crane-730 on 2026-11-11 (rulings A, B, C) and the seam agreed with merry-seal-673: the door owns
// composition and the credential brackets; THIS module owns the carrier reads, the decoders, and the
// capture verdicts. The door hands this mint the PATHS its brackets minted (one 0600 password file used
// via `-f`, never argv; one netrc) — never secret bytes — and runs it inside the held arrival slot.
//
// WHAT MAKES A CAPTURE HONEST HERE:
//  * Every response is committed through gunbc.provider_wire_evidence.retain_private_evidence_bytes_detailed
//    and READ BACK before it is decoded; the CarrierCapture is assembled from the READ-BACK bytes, so the
//    archive claim is re-checkable from the store, not from a value that evaporated with the call.
//    (No second BmcSuppliedResponse mint exists — commit_captured_response stays the sole mint in
//    gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_account_state_live, per the seam; the raw bytes ride the same evidence
//    discipline directly, and this module's OWN rows are the carrier verdicts keyed by content digest.)
//  * A carrier whose read failed for a NON-authenticated transport reason REFUSES the whole mint
//    (LiveCaptureRefused): a half-read prior life must not reach the classifier dressed up as gaps.
//    Gaps are reserved for what the controller ANSWERED and could not serve (typed CarrierGapCause), and
//    an empty list appears only when the controller SERVED an empty collection — never fabricated.
//  * STOP ON FIRST AUTH REFUSAL (smart-crane-730, 2026-11-11): the first IpmiSessionAuthRefused or
//    401-class Redfish refusal ends the mint immediately. A rejected managed credential means every later
//    op would fail too; continuing only burns srv15's lockout budget. Rows already committed stay
//    readable from the store — the refusal arm carries them — but no further authenticated op is issued.
//  * Read-only ops only: every op here is declared `readonly` at its module; no account write, no BIOS
//    write, no boot-parameter SET, no SEL/LogService clearing POST. The retry bound is pinned in the
//    shared authenticated templates of extdeps.bmc/ipmi.dag (`-R 1 -N 1`), so the worst case per
//    invocation is 2 failed authentications, and the door's gate compares THAT against the served
//    Bad Password Threshold. Redfish rides one curl invocation per op with no auth retry (curl(1) does
//    not retry a 401 unless asked; these argv never ask).
//
// THE FLEET-SPECIFIC BINDINGS (log-services path, audit service id, chassis id, VirtualMedia parent) are
// PARAMETERS: the door passes the values its platform context knows (for srv15:
// "/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices", the audit log service's served Id, asrock_altrad8ud_redfish_chassis_id,
// UnderSystem { system_id: "system" }). This module stays platform-neutral so the ALTRAD8UD row of
// gunbc.machine_intake.prior_life_boundary — not a reader constant — remains the authority on what is
// required; the row is swift-ram-509's single authority, carrying the operator's ruling msg_9ed289f6
// ("Admit uncleared, archive only", escalation msg_9a98f6c6-1d7e-431a-b4c7-91d632558be1).

